    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "On the difference between [womotte1] and [womotte2]\n[womotte1] is a Time phrase\nmeaning \"at\" - marks beginnings, ends, or borders between times.\nIt is often used as a greeting to お客 with the extended form をもちまして.\n[womotte2] is the method by which you do something - victory achieved via effort, announcement made via a blackboard.\n\nBoth are formal, both are NOUN + をもって\nbe careful.",
      "html": "<b>On the difference between [womotte1] and [womotte2]</b><br/>[womotte1] is a Time phrase<br/>meaning \"at\" - marks beginnings, ends, or borders between times.<br/>It is often used as a greeting to お客 with the extended form をもちまして.<br/>[womotte2] is the method by which you do something - victory achieved via effort, announcement made via a blackboard.<br/><br/>Both are formal, both are NOUN + をもって<br/>be careful.",
      "credits_raw": "LR",
      "content_sha256": "97da2403c137e1c72cf9537a31e619b9a2133e52e370e885f853b0b172a0ed78",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
